🏠 Scenario:

You have 3 rooms.

Each room has 1 bulb.

Outside the rooms, you have 3 switches (buttons) (one switch controls one bulb).

You can enter the rooms only once to check bulbs.

You need to figure out which switch controls which bulb.

🔦 Trick Solution:

Turn ON switch 1 and leave it ON for a few minutes.
(This will make the bulb in that room hot 🔥).

Turn OFF switch 1 and then turn ON switch 2.

Leave switch 3 OFF.

🚪 Now enter the rooms:

The bulb that is ON → belongs to switch 2.

The bulb that is OFF but HOT → belongs to switch 1.

The bulb that is OFF and COLD → belongs to switch 3.

✅ This way you can map all switches to bulbs in just one visit.